# Visual system

## Current interface evidence
Reference observed screens, components and design tokens.

## Design intent and constraints
Tie the visual direction and hierarchy to evidenced user tasks, brand, and approved preferences; mark new choices Proposed with a rationale.

## Design tokens
Provide a token/value/status/source table for semantic colors, typography, spacing, layout, shape, and motion. Verify contrast rather than claiming it by intent.

## Layout, components and iconography
Describe task-specific page hierarchy, responsive layout, component reuse, icon source and consistent icon rules. Avoid decorative or unsupported elements.

## Component and state rules
Cover applicable responsive behavior, interaction states, keyboard/focus, screen-reader names, error recovery, and reduced motion.

## Visual review checklist
Record a rendered review at representative viewports when implementation/prototype exists; otherwise mark visual verification Not run. Check hierarchy, consistency, responsiveness, accessibility, and evidence-backed content.

## Not applicable or unresolved
Give the technical reason for a headless project's lack of visual UI.
